# Responsive UI

Any UI change must work on **PC, laptop, tablet, and mobile**. Do not ship desktop-only layouts.

## Required checks

Before finishing UI work, verify (or adjust CSS for) roughly:

| Class | Width | Expectations |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PC / large laptop | ≥981px | Full sidebar layout, multi-column grids |
| Laptop / small desktop | ~861–980px | Overview may collapse; avoid overflow |
| Tablet / large phone | ≤860px | Sidebar → five-tab bar + More sheet; stack panels; tap targets ≥44px |
| Phone | ≤560px | Single column; readable type; no horizontal scroll |

Match existing breakpoints in `src/frontend/styles/ledger.css` (`980px`, `860px`, `560px`) unless a new query is clearly needed.

## Patterns

```css
/* ❌ BAD — fixed width that breaks on phone */
.panel { width: 720px; }

/* ✅ GOOD — fluid + existing breakpoints */
.panel { width: 100%; max-width: 720px; }
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .panel { padding: 12px; }
}
```

- Prefer fluid widths (`%`, `minmax(0, 1fr)`, `min-width: 0`) over fixed pixel shells.
- Stack grids/flex rows at tablet/mobile; don’t clip labels or force overflow.
- Modals, pickers, and toolbars must remain usable on small screens and touch (`hover: none`).
- When editing a component, update the matching `@media` rules in `ledger.css` in the same change.
